---
// Added 2026-10-01 at the owner's request (AUTH.md section 12.6): the form can also be opened by
// the event site.contact.openEvent, sent on the document by any script - today the sign-in page,
// when a visitor presses "Помощь" or "Написать в поддержку" in Clerk's form. The event's name
// reaches the inline script below through data-open-event, since an inline script cannot import
// the config; its detail may carry `email` and `subject` to fill in.
//
// Restyled the same day at the owner's request: the form takes the site's look in both themes,
// the values Clerk's forms were given in src/styles/clerk.css and the site's own buttons
// (src/pages/auth/account.astro, PaidVideo.astro). It used zinc greys and an emerald button,
// which no other part of the site uses; in the dark theme its fields were grey on a dark-blue
// card. The classes it had, so the change can be followed or undone:
//   card     rounded-2xl border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-900 (bg-white kept)
//   close    text-zinc-400 hover:text-zinc-600 dark:hover:text-zinc-200
//   heading  text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100
//   labels   text-xs text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400
//   fields   rounded-xl border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 focus:border-emerald-500 dark:border-zinc-700
//            dark:bg-zinc-800
//   button   rounded-xl bg-emerald-600 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium shadow-md transition-colors
//            hover:bg-emerald-700
//   toast    bg-emerald-600 on success
// What they are now, and where each comes from:
//   card     rounded-lg like every card on the site, gray-200 / slate-700 border. Its background
//            was already --panel-bg in both themes: custom.css paints .bg-white with !important,
//            so dark:bg-zinc-900 never applied and is gone.
//   heading  gray-800 / gray-200, Clerk's foreground colours.
//   labels   text-sm, the size of the labels in Clerk's forms, gray-500 / slate-400.
//   fields   white with a gray-300 border, slate-800 with a slate-700 border in the dark theme,
//            text gray-800 / gray-200, and a blue-600 (dark: blue-500) border and ring on focus -
//            the input colours in clerk.css. White is bg-[#ffffff]: plain bg-white would be
//            repainted to --panel-bg by custom.css and the fields would melt into the card.
//   button   the site's button exactly - rounded bg-blue-600 px-4 py-2 text-white, opacity on
//            hover - at full width.
//   toast    green-600 on success, the pinned palette's green; red-600 on an error, as before.
//
// Added later the same day at the owner's request (AUTH.md section 12.7): for a signed-in member
// the form fills in the name, when Clerk's profile has one, and the email, however it is opened;
// the message is left to the member. The two come from localStorage under site.auth.contactKey
// (data-member-key below), which the pages that load Clerk write next to the session flag, since
// this form is on every page and must not load Clerk. The three fields carry ym-disable-keys, so
// that Yandex Metrika's Session Replay does not record what is in them.
// Changed 2026-10-12 (T167, the removal of the previous sign-in provider): the name and the email come from
// `GET /api/auth/me` and not from a localStorage record; `data-member-key` and `site.auth.contactKey` are gone.
//
// Changed 2026-10-13 (T109, plan phase 7): the form posts to the club's own route, `POST /api/feedback`
// (server/src/feedback/routes.ts), and no longer to the external web3forms service; its access key is gone from the
// markup. The look, the open event and the toasts are as they were. What changed, and why:
// - The body is JSON, built by the script from the three fields: `message` is the route's `body`, `name` its `name`,
//   `email` its `contact`, and the hidden subject field, when the form was opened by the event with a topic, its
//   `subject` (a code of the fixed list in src/lib/feedback-rules.ts, not text).
// - A honeypot field named `website`, off-screen and out of the tab order and of the screen reader's reach: a person
//   never fills it, a form-filling bot does, and the route then refuses with the same plain 400 as for a form sent
//   too fast. It carries no label text on purpose (nothing visible, nothing to translate).
// - `startedAt`, the moment the form was opened, in the SERVER's time: the device's clock may be minutes off, and the
//   route refuses a form that is "from the future" or older than a day. The offset is learned from the Date header of
//   the `/api/auth/me` answer the form asks for when it opens (the way the panel's scripts learn it, auth-forms.ts), and
//   added to the moment of opening when the form is sent. A device whose clock is a long way off therefore still sends.
// - The `maxlength` of each field is the route's own limit (src/lib/feedback-rules.ts), so the browser stops the typing
//   before the server has to refuse it.
// - A third toast, for the route's 429 (five stored messages an hour from one address): "too many messages, try
//   later", where a refusal of any other kind keeps the general "sending failed".
// - The submit button is disabled while a message is on its way, so a double press stores one message.
import { site } from "../config";
// Added 2026-10-13 (T109): the lengths of the three texts, the route's own.
import { feedbackTextLimits } from "../lib/feedback-rules";
// Added 2026-10-12 at the owner's request (the interface in two languages, src/i18n/lang.ts): every
// label of the form in both languages through T, and the two toasts as templates the inline script
// clones, since an inline script cannot import the dictionary. The subject the sign-in page sends
// stays Russian: it is read by whoever receives the letter, not by the visitor.
import { ui } from "../i18n/strings";
import T from "./T.astro";
---

<div
  id="contact-modal"
  class="fixed inset-0 z-50 hidden items-center justify-center bg-black/60 p-4 backdrop-blur-sm"
  data-open-event={site.contact.openEvent}
>
  <!-- Контейнер модалки -->
  <div
    class="relative w-full max-w-md rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-2xl dark:border-slate-700"
  >
    <!-- Кнопка закрытия -->
    <button
      id="close-modal-btn"
      class="absolute right-4 top-4 text-xl text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-600 dark:text-slate-400 dark:hover:text-gray-200"
    >
      ✕
    </button>

    {
      /* Changed 2026-09-30, from a Tailwind 3.4 audit the owner ordered: font-bilingual, the site's
      serif, where it was font-serif. The config never sets `serif`, so that class gave Tailwind's
      default stack (Georgia and the like) and the heading stood apart from every other heading
      on the site (Font Family, "Customizing your theme"). */
    }
    <h3
      class="mb-4 font-bilingual text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200"
    >
      {
        /* Changed 2026-10-12: both languages (it read "Обратная связь"); so are the labels below. */
      }
      <T s={ui.contact_title} />
    </h3>

    {
      /* Changed 2026-10-13 (T109): the form's address is the club's own route and it has an id of its own (the
      script looked it up by the old service's address); the service's access key input is gone. The script
      sends JSON, so without it the form would only post urlencoded text the route refuses - which is why the
      address is not a way to send, only a place for a browser that has no script to fail without leaking the
      message into the address bar. */
    }
    <form
      id="contact-form"
      action="/api/feedback"
      method="POST"
      class="space-y-4"
    >
      {
        /* Added 2026-10-01 (AUTH.md section 12.6): the subject of the letter, web3forms' `subject`
        field ("The Name attribute must be called subject", web3forms docs, "Email Subject line").
        Disabled, and therefore not sent, unless the form was opened by the open event with a
        subject - "Проблема со входом" from the sign-in page; opened from the footer, the letter
        keeps web3forms' own subject as before. */
      }

      {
        /* Added 2026-10-01 at the owner's request: ym-disable-keys on the three fields below, Yandex
        Metrika's class that keeps a field's contents out of Session Replay (the Webvisor) - replaced
        with asterisks in the recording (Yandex's help, "Enabling and configuring Session Replay";
        METRIKA.md proposal 3.1, which covers this form). Needed now that a member's name and email
        are filled in by themselves (fillMember in the script below), not only typed. */
      }
      <input
        id="contact-subject"
        type="hidden"
        name="subject"
        value=""
        disabled
      />

      <div>
        <label class="mb-1 block text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400"
          ><T s={ui.contact_name} /></label
        >
        <input
          type="text"
          name="name"
          required
          maxlength={feedbackTextLimits.maxNameChars}
          class="ym-disable-keys w-full rounded border border-gray-300 bg-[#ffffff] p-2.5 text-sm text-gray-800 focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-none focus:ring-1 focus:ring-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-gray-200 dark:focus:border-blue-500 dark:focus:ring-blue-500"
        />
      </div>

      <div>
        <label class="mb-1 block text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400"
          ><T s={ui.contact_email} /></label
        >
        <input
          type="email"
          name="email"
          required
          maxlength={feedbackTextLimits.maxContactChars}
          class="ym-disable-keys w-full rounded border border-gray-300 bg-[#ffffff] p-2.5 text-sm text-gray-800 focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-none focus:ring-1 focus:ring-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-gray-200 dark:focus:border-blue-500 dark:focus:ring-blue-500"
        />
      </div>

      <div>
        <label class="mb-1 block text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-slate-400"
          ><T s={ui.contact_message} /></label
        >
        <textarea
          name="message"
          rows="4"
          required
          maxlength={feedbackTextLimits.maxBodyChars}
          class="ym-disable-keys w-full rounded border border-gray-300 bg-[#ffffff] p-2.5 text-sm text-gray-800 focus:border-blue-600 focus:outline-none focus:ring-1 focus:ring-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-gray-200 dark:focus:border-blue-500 dark:focus:ring-blue-500"
        ></textarea>
      </div>

      {
        /* Added 2026-10-13 (T109): the honeypot (the note at the top). Off-screen by the sr-only class, out of the tab
        order and hidden from assistive technology; a visitor never sees or reaches it. */
      }
      <div class="sr-only" aria-hidden="true">
        <input
          type="text"
          name="website"
          tabindex="-1"
          autocomplete="off"
          value=""
        />
      </div>

      <button
        type="submit"
        class="w-full rounded bg-blue-600 px-4 py-2 text-white transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
      >
        <T s={ui.contact_send} />
      </button>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>

{
  /* Added 2026-10-12: the two toasts' texts in both languages (the note at the top); showToast()
  below clones one into the toast, and custom.css shows the language of the page. */
}
<template id="contact-toast-sent"><T s={ui.contact_sent} /></template>
<template id="contact-toast-failed"><T s={ui.contact_failed} /></template>
<template id="contact-toast-limit"><T s={ui.contact_limit} /></template>

<!-- Контейнер для toast-уведомлений -->
<div
  id="toast-container"
  class="pointer-events-none fixed bottom-6 right-6 z-[60] flex flex-col gap-2"
>
</div>

<script is:inline>
  const modal = document.getElementById("contact-modal");
  const openBtn = document.getElementById("open-modal-btn");
  const closeBtn = document.getElementById("close-modal-btn");
  // Changed 2026-10-13 (T109): the form has an id of its own; it was found by the old service's address.
  const form = document.getElementById("contact-form");
  const toastContainer = document.getElementById("toast-container");

  // Универсальная функция toast
  function showToast(message, type = "success") {
    const colors = {
      // Changed 2026-10-01 (the restyle noted at the top): green-600, the site's green, was emerald-600.
      success: "bg-green-600",
      error: "bg-red-600",
    };

    const toast = document.createElement("div");
    toast.className = `
      pointer-events-auto
      flex items-center gap-3
      rounded-xl px-4 py-3
      text-sm font-medium text-white
      shadow-lg
      opacity-0 translate-y-3
      transition-all duration-300 ease-out
      ${colors[type]}
    `;
    // Changed 2026-10-12: the message is a template's id now (contact-toast-sent or -failed), whose
    // content holds the text in both languages; it was a string put into the second span with
    // innerHTML: <span>${message}</span>.
    toast.innerHTML = `
      <span>${type === "success" ? "✓" : "✕"}</span>
    `;
    const text = document.createElement("span");
    const template = document.getElementById(message);
    if (template instanceof HTMLTemplateElement) {
      text.append(template.content.cloneNode(true));
    }
    toast.append(text);

    toastContainer.appendChild(toast);

    // анимация появления
    requestAnimationFrame(() => {
      toast.classList.remove("opacity-0", "translate-y-3");
    });

    // автоскрытие
    setTimeout(() => {
      toast.classList.add("opacity-0", "translate-y-3");
      setTimeout(() => toast.remove(), 300);
    }, 3500);
  }

  // Модалка открыть
  openBtn?.addEventListener("click", () => {
    modal?.classList.remove("hidden");
    modal?.classList.add("flex");
  });

  // Added 2026-10-01 (AUTH.md section 12.6): the second way in, the open event (its name is in
  // data-open-event on the modal, from site.contact.openEvent). The detail may give an email
  // address, written only into an empty field so that nothing the visitor typed is overwritten,
  // and a subject, which switches the hidden subject field on.
  const emailInput = form?.querySelector('input[name="email"]');
  const subjectInput = document.getElementById("contact-subject");
  const openEvent = modal?.dataset.openEvent;

  // Added 2026-10-01 at the owner's request (AUTH.md section 12.7): for a member, the name and the email in the
  // form, written only into empty fields while the document is marked kb-member; the message is left to the visitor.
  // (Corrected 2026-10-12, T167: the source is the club's own backend, see fillMember below. The first version read a
  // record kept by the previous sign-in provider's pages, which is gone.)
  const nameInput = form?.querySelector('input[name="name"]');
  // Changed 2026-10-12 (T167, the removal of the previous sign-in provider): the name and the email now come from the
  // club's own backend (`GET /api/auth/me`, the same answer the account pages use), not from a localStorage record the
  // provider's pages used to keep; nothing writes that record any more. Asked only while the document is marked
  // kb-member, which the server sets from the session; a failed ask leaves the fields as they are.
  // Changed 2026-10-13 (T109): called at every opening of the form, it now also (1) records the moment of opening, the
  // route's `startedAt`, and (2) learns how far this device's clock is from the server's, from the Date header of the
  // answer; both are used when the form is sent (sendMessage below). So the question is asked of every visitor, not
  // only of a member as before: a visitor's answer is `{"viewer": null}` and fills nothing, and without it a device
  // whose clock is minutes off would be refused as a bot or a stale form. A failed ask leaves the offset at zero.
  let openedAt = Date.now();
  let clockOffset = 0;
  function fillMember() {
    openedAt = Date.now();
    fetch("/api/auth/me", {
      headers: { Accept: "application/json" },
      credentials: "same-origin",
    })
      .then((response) => {
        const served = Date.parse(response.headers.get("Date") || "");
        if (!Number.isNaN(served)) clockOffset = served - Date.now();
        return response.json();
      })
      .then((body) => {
        const member = body && body.viewer;
        if (!member || typeof member !== "object") return;
        if (
          nameInput &&
          !nameInput.value &&
          typeof member.displayName === "string"
        ) {
          nameInput.value = member.displayName;
        }
        if (
          emailInput &&
          !emailInput.value &&
          typeof member.email === "string"
        ) {
          emailInput.value = member.email;
        }
      })
      .catch(() => {});
  }

  if (openEvent) {
    document.addEventListener(openEvent, (event) => {
      const detail =
        event instanceof CustomEvent && event.detail ? event.detail : {};
      if (emailInput && !emailInput.value && typeof detail.email === "string") {
        emailInput.value = detail.email;
      }
      // Added with fillMember above: after the event's own email, so an address the sender gave wins.
      fillMember();
      if (subjectInput) {
        subjectInput.value =
          typeof detail.subject === "string" ? detail.subject : "";
        subjectInput.disabled = subjectInput.value === "";
      }
      modal?.classList.remove("hidden");
      modal?.classList.add("flex");
    });
  }
  // Added with it: opened from the footer button, the form sends no subject, as before, even if
  // the open event had switched it on earlier on this page. A listener of its own, next to the
  // button's original one above.
  openBtn?.addEventListener("click", () => {
    if (subjectInput) subjectInput.disabled = true;
    // Added with fillMember above: a member opening the form from the footer gets it filled too.
    fillMember();
  });

  // закрыть
  closeBtn?.addEventListener("click", () => {
    modal?.classList.remove("flex");
    modal?.classList.add("hidden");
  });

  // закрыть так же при клике на полупрозрачный фон вокруг формы
  modal?.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
    if (e.target === modal) {
      modal.classList.remove("flex");
      modal.classList.add("hidden");
    }
  });

  // Отправка формы
  // Changed 2026-10-13 (T109): the form is sent as JSON to the club's own route (the note at the top of the file lists
  // the mapping of the fields); it was a FormData post to web3forms. The submit button is off while a message is on its
  // way, and the route's 429 has a toast of its own.
  let sending = false;
  if (form) {
    form.addEventListener("submit", async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      if (sending) return;
      sending = true;
      const sendButton = form.querySelector('button[type="submit"]');
      if (sendButton) sendButton.disabled = true;

      const field = (name) => {
        const element = form.elements.namedItem(name);
        return element && "value" in element ? String(element.value) : "";
      };
      const message = {
        body: field("message"),
        name: field("name"),
        contact: field("email"),
        website: field("website"),
        // The moment of opening in the SERVER's time (the note at fillMember above).
        startedAt: openedAt + clockOffset,
      };
      // The topic is sent only when the open event gave one; opened from the footer the form names none.
      if (subjectInput && !subjectInput.disabled && subjectInput.value !== "") {
        message.subject = subjectInput.value;
      }

      try {
        const response = await fetch("/api/feedback", {
          method: "POST",
          headers: {
            "Content-Type": "application/json",
            Accept: "application/json",
          },
          credentials: "same-origin",
          body: JSON.stringify(message),
        });

        if (response.ok) {
          form.reset(); // очистить форму
          modal.classList.add("hidden");
          modal.classList.remove("flex");
          // Changed 2026-10-12 here and in the two calls below: the template's id (showToast's note);
          // the texts were "Сообщение отправлено!" and "Ошибка отправки. Попробуйте ещё раз.".
          showToast("contact-toast-sent", "success");
        } else if (response.status === 429) {
          showToast("contact-toast-limit", "error");
        } else {
          showToast("contact-toast-failed", "error");
        }
      } catch (error) {
        console.error(error);
        showToast("contact-toast-failed", "error");
      } finally {
        sending = false;
        if (sendButton) sendButton.disabled = false;
      }
    });
  }

  // страховка от bfcache при возврате "назад"
  window.addEventListener("pageshow", () => {
    form?.reset();
  });
</script>
